# Copy to deploy/.env (git-ignored) and fill in. Never commit deploy/.env.
#
# Compose reads this file only to fill the ${...} placeholders in docker-compose.yml.
# It is not passed into the containers, and it is unrelated to backend/.env (which the
# containers never see).

# Which tunnel runs next to the demo:
#   quick  random https://<words>.trycloudflare.com address, no Cloudflare account needed;
#          the address changes on every start (docker compose logs tunnel)
#   named  fixed hostname from your Cloudflare account (fill in the two values below)
#   empty  no tunnel: the demo is only reachable at http://127.0.0.1:8010 on this PC
COMPOSE_PROFILES=quick

# --- Named tunnel only -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Token of the tunnel (Cloudflare Zero Trust > Networks > Tunnels > your tunnel). A secret:
# it lets anyone run your tunnel. Keep it in this file only.
TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# Public hostname of the tunnel, without https:// (for example demo.example.com). In the
# dashboard its service must be http://demo:8000. Leave empty for the quick tunnel.
DEMO_HOSTNAME=

# --- Optional --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port on this PC's loopback (127.0.0.1) for checking the demo locally.
# DEMO_LOCAL_PORT=8010
# /api requests one visitor address may send per minute.
# DEMO_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=120
# SEC EDGAR asks for a User-Agent of the form "app-name contact-email". Empty: the demo
# skips the 13F investors (ARK still works). It is your contact address: decide yourself.
# DEMO_SEC_USER_AGENT=
# First three numbers of the demo network. Change it if Docker reports that the address
# range overlaps another network.
# DEMO_SUBNET_PREFIX=172.30.35
# What the first start does when the demo ledger cannot be priced (no network, provider
# blocked): abort = do not serve, retry after a pause (default); continue = serve an empty
# ledger. Synthetic prices are never used either way.
# DEMO_SEED_ON_FAILURE=abort
